      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture of the test. The main issues are:\n1. Repeated code for the \"get specifier → convert to bytes → reconstruct codec\" pattern (appears 4 times)\n2. Unused imports and unused static data-provider methods (dead code with no `@ParameterizedTest` annotations)\n3. Sparse comments that don't explain the four distinct scenarios being tested\n4. Magic bounds `> 116` / `< 141` with no context\n\nI'll extract the repetitive roundtrip logic into a helper, remove dead code, and add clear scenario labels.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version extracts the repeated specifier-roundtrip logic into a `roundTripRunCodec` helper, removes all dead code (unused static data-provider methods and their imports), and labels each of the four scenarios with clear comments explaining what makes each case distinct."
    }
